    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dc1f44e6-2b7d-5aa3-8a26-e1a2bca35e79",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $det(A)=4$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=7 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=4$, so $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=7$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is true. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ is true. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$ is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A\\text{ is invertible}$; $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ only.",
